    {
      "id": "f3a7555c-f378-4790-a8b2-7803b1db69eb",
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "Found the bug: notebook cell `63c1fe60` imports `load_flare_config` from `downstream_apps.template.configs`, but this app has its own `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs.py` with a `FlareDataConfig` that adds `mask_dir` and `mask_time_tolerance` fields (used later in the notebook for mask alignment). The template's version doesn't have those fields, so loading the YAML through it raises \"Unrecognized key(s)\". The dataset import in a later cell already correctly points to `downstream_apps.sf_triggers.datasets.sf_triggers_dataset` \u2014 only the config import cell is wrong.",
      "mentions": [],
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789487282.0560417
    },
    {
      "body": "",
