            "raw_input": {
              "content": "# Fix wrong config import in sf_triggers notebook\n\n## Context\n\n`downstream_apps/sf_triggers/0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb` cell `63c1fe60` fails with:\n\n```\nValueError: Unrecognized key(s) in 'data:' section of the config: mask_dir, mask_time_tolerance.\nValid keys for FlareDataConfig are: channels, ds_match_direction, ... (no mask_dir/mask_time_tolerance)\n```\n\n`configs/config_script.yaml` legitimately sets `mask_dir` and `mask_time_tolerance` under `data:` \u2014 these drive the SHARP bitmap mask alignment used later in the notebook. The sf_triggers app already has its own `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs.py::FlareDataConfig`, which *does* declare both fields (and adds `mask_dir` to `PATH_FIELDS` for path resolution). The notebook cell, however, imports `load_flare_config` from `downstream_apps.template.configs` \u2014 the generic template's version, which only has the original four flare-alignment fields and knows nothing about masks. That mismatch is the entire bug; every other cell in the notebook (e.g. the `FlareDSDataset` import) already correctly points at the `sf_triggers` app.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb`, cell `63c1fe60`, change:\n\n```python\nfrom downstream_apps.template.configs import load_flare_config\n```\n\nto:\n\n```python\nfrom downstream_apps.sf_triggers.configs import load_flare_config\n```\n\nNo other changes needed \u2014 `downstream_apps/sf_triggers/configs.py` already has the right fields.\n\n## Verification\n\nRun the notebook cell(s) via the Jupyter MCP tools (`read_notebook_cells` to confirm the edit landed, then `run_cell` on `63c1fe60`) and confirm:\n- No `ValueError` is raised.\n- `Loaded config for job: solar_flare_forecasting` prints, along with resolved train index / scalers paths.\n\nThen optionally run the rest of the notebook top-to-bottom (`run_all_cells`) to make sure downstream cells (which rely on `cfg.data.mask_dir` indirectly through `FlareDSDataset`) still behave as before.\n",
